<h1>From an app to a Worker</h1>
<p class="lead">Five steps. The first is done once per Soli version; the others are your
everyday loop.</p>

<ol class="steps">
  <li>
    <h2>Build the edge runtime</h2>
    <p>In the Soli source tree. It needs the wasm32 target and the wasm-bindgen CLI at the
       version <code>edge/Cargo.toml</code> pins; the script says which if they are missing.</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version 0.2.126 --locked
./scripts/build-edge.sh          # → target/edge</code></pre>
  </li>
  <li>
    <h2>Package your app</h2>
    <p>From the app folder. <code>app/</code>, <code>config/</code> and <code>lib/</code> go into
       the Worker; <code>public/</code> becomes its static assets; <code>.env</code> stays out.</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">export SOLI_EDGE_RUNTIME=~/soli/target/edge
soli edge build                  # → dist/edge</code></pre>
    <p><code>dist/edge</code> is a plain Wrangler project. Its <code>wrangler.toml</code> is
       written once; later builds keep your edits.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <h2>Run it on workerd</h2>
<pre><code class="language-bash">cd dist/edge
npx wrangler dev                 # http://localhost:8787</code></pre>
    <p>That is Cloudflare's own runtime, locally: what works here works deployed.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <h2>Configure it</h2>
    <p>Everything your app reads with <code>getenv()</code> comes from the Worker's
       bindings: plain values under <code>[vars]</code> in <code>wrangler.toml</code>, secrets
       with Wrangler.</p>
<pre><code class="language-toml">[vars]
SOLIDB_HOST = "https://db.example.com"
SOLIDB_DATABASE = "my_app"
SOLIDB_USERNAME = "app"</code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-bash">npx wrangler secret put SOLIDB_PASSWORD</code></pre>
    <p>For data that lives with the Worker, use D1: create a database, bind it, and
       point the models at it.</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">npx wrangler d1 create my-app-db     # prints the database_id</code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-toml">[[d1_databases]]
binding = "DB"
database_name = "my-app-db"
database_id = "…"

[vars]
SOLI_DB_ADAPTER = "d1"</code></pre>
    <p>The app can tell where it runs: <code>getenv("SOLI_RUNTIME")</code> is
       <code>"cloudflare-workers"</code> there.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <h2>Deploy</h2>
<pre><code class="language-bash">npx wrangler deploy</code></pre>
    <p>For your own domain, once its zone is on the same Cloudflare account, add to
       <code>wrangler.toml</code>:</p>
<pre><code class="language-toml">routes = [{ pattern = "app.example.com", custom_domain = true }]</code></pre>
  </li>
</ol>
